To organize the conditions in the `conditions.ml` file similar to the structure in the `commons.ml` file (where each condition type is represented as a list or structure), we need to create individual components for each group of conditions (pop_conditions, country_conditions, province_conditions, and state_conditions) and structure them accordingly. 

Below is an example of how you might reorganize the `conditions.ml` file into a structured format that reflects the organization seen in `commons.ml`.

```ocaml
(* conditions.ml *)

open SymbolTable
open TypeDef

let pop_conditions = [
  (
    "is_canal_enabled",
    PARAM_VALUE(INT)
  );
  (
    "agree_with_ruling_party",
    PARAM_VALUE(FLOAT)
  );
  (
    "cash_reserves",
    PARAM_VALUE(INT)
  );
  (
    "consciousness",
    PARAM_OPTION([
      PARAM_VALUE(FLOAT);
      PARAM_VALUE(INT)
    ])
  );
  (
    "culture",
    PARAM_VALUE(KEYWORD)
  );
  (
    "everyday_needs",
    PARAM_OPTION([
      PARAM_VALUE(FLOAT);
      PARAM_VALUE(INT)
    ])
  );
  (
    "has_pop_culture",
    PARAM_VALUE(KEYWORD)
  );
  (
    "has_pop_religion",
    PARAM_VALUE(KEYWORD)
  );
  (
    "is_primary_culture",
    PARAM_OPTION([
      PARAM_VALUE(KEYWORD);
      PARAM_VALUE(TAG);
      PARAM_VALUE(SCOPE);
      PARAM_VALUE(BOOL)
    ])
  );
  (
    "always",
    PARAM_VALUE(BOOL)
  );
  (* Add remaining conditions similarly *)
]

let country_conditions = [
  (
    "always",
    PARAM_VALUE(BOOL)
  );
  (
    "overlord",
    SubTable "country_conditions"
  );
  (
    "produces",
    PARAM_VALUE(KEYWORD)
  );
  (* Add remaining conditions similarly *)
]

let province_conditions = [
  (
    "can_build_in_province",
    PARAM_LIST (symbol_table_init [
      (KEYWORD_SYMBOL("building"), PARAM_VALUE(KEYWORD));
      (KEYWORD_SYMBOL("limit_to_world_greatest_level"), PARAM_VALUE(BOOL))
    ])
  );
  (
    "has_global_flag",
    PARAM_VALUE(KEYWORD)
  );
  (
    "state_scope",
    SubTable "state_conditions"
  );
  (* Add remaining conditions similarly *)
]

let state_conditions = [
  (
    "is_canal_enabled",
    PARAM_VALUE(INT)
  );
  (
    "infrastructure",
    PARAM_VALUE(KEYWORD)
  );
  (
    "produces",
    PARAM_VALUE(KEYWORD)
  );
  (* Add remaining conditions similarly *)
]
```

This structure organizes each group of conditions as a list of tuples, with the condition name and its corresponding parameters. It modularizes your conditions similarly to how definitions are structured in `commons.ml`, making the file easier to manage and understand. Each list represents a particular type or category of conditions, allowing for better separation and organization of data.
